From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 07:33:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] msm8996-common: label the pmi8994 LPG channels so hal_light
 is not denied

hal_light enumerates /sys/class/leds at startup and reads max_brightness and
trigger on the pmi8994 leds@d000 channels, a sibling of the haptics node that
was already labelled. Only the label was missing, so every read was denied:

  avc: denied { read } name="max_brightness" scontext=u:r:hal_light_default:s0
       tcontext=u:object_r:sysfs:s0 tclass=file

Nine denials a boot. hal_light already holds rw_file_perms on sysfs_leds in
system sepolicy, so labelling the directory removes them.

No LED is attached to those channels. The V20 has no notification LED and uses
the second screen for notifications; the node is inherited from the PMI8994
reference device tree and the qpnp driver binds to it regardless. Writes to
brightness are accepted and read back at 255 with nothing illuminating, which
is what a PMIC LPG output with nothing wired to it does. max_brightness
reporting 255 and writes succeeding are properties of the driver, not evidence
of an LED.

This labels the nodes so the denials stop. It does not light anything, and
nothing should be built on top of it expecting a notification light.
---
 sepolicy/vendor/genfs_contexts | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sepolicy/vendor/genfs_contexts b/sepolicy/vendor/genfs_contexts
index e45ec891..1ad0c097 100644
--- a/sepolicy/vendor/genfs_contexts
+++ b/sepolicy/vendor/genfs_contexts
@@ -43,5 +43,11 @@ genfscon sysfs /devices/soc/75b5000.i2c/i2c-7/7-001d/power_supply   u:object_r:s
 # LEDs
 genfscon sysfs /devices/soc/400f000.qcom,spmi/spmi-0/spmi0-03/400f000.qcom,spmi:qcom,pmi8994@3:qcom,haptics@c000/leds/vibrator   u:object_r:sysfs_leds:s0
 genfscon sysfs /devices/soc/74a4900.sdhci/leds                                                                                    u:object_r:sysfs_leds:s0
+# The pmi8994 LPG channels, a sibling of the haptics node above. No LED is wired to them on this
+# hardware: the V20 has no notification LED and uses the second screen instead. The node comes from
+# the PMI8994 reference device tree and hal_light still enumerates it at startup, so without this
+# label the nodes stay u:object_r:sysfs:s0 and hal_light is denied reading max_brightness and
+# trigger. Labelling only silences those denials; it does not light anything.
+genfscon sysfs /devices/soc/400f000.qcom,spmi/spmi-0/spmi0-03/400f000.qcom,spmi:qcom,pmi8994@3:qcom,leds@d000/leds   u:object_r:sysfs_leds:s0
 
 # ProcFS
